      <dataObjectReference id="dataObjectReference_1ae66ac8-5689-4393-9871-a4ea6064e065"
                            name="Exception notification and investigation evidence"
                            dataObjectRef="_1ae66ac8-5689-4393-9871-a4ea6064e065">
         <documentation id="documentation_1ae66ac8-5689-4393-9871-a4ea6064e065"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004; CSP-PR-005; CSP-ST-007; CSP-PR-008.
 
Producer: Settlement Operations.
 
Consumers: Trade Operations, assigned exception owners and relevant operational, accounting and reconciliation teams.
 
Content: Affected trade and version references, currency legs, known instruction identifiers and statuses, investigation findings, communications, attempted corrective or recovery actions, supporting evidence, cut-off impact, outstanding obligations, assigned owner, next action and follow-up time.
 
Purpose: Supports escalation and continued management of unresolved preparation, submission, settlement or recovery exceptions.
 
Preserve confirmed settlement history and distinguish verified outcomes from missing or uncertain information. The notification records ownership and follow-up arrangements; it does not itself confirm successful settlement or completion of recovery.]]></documentation>
