      <dataObjectReference id="dataObjectReference_9014c752-253b-4508-b8ed-25c7273c71eb"
                            name="Daily maturity population"
                            dataObjectRef="_9014c752-253b-4508-b8ed-25c7273c71eb">
         <documentation id="documentation_9014c752-253b-4508-b8ed-25c7273c71eb"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004; CSP-ST-001; CSP-ST-002.
 
Purpose: Daily SYS-FAP output identifying trades requiring maturity preparation or continued operational follow-up after their contractual value date.
 
Content: trade_id, trade_version, contractual value date, business_days_to_maturity, and maturity_status. The population covers the five-business-day preparation window and matured positions that remain operationally incomplete.
 
Status interpretation: UPCOMING indicates a future contractual value date within the preparation window. MATURED indicates that the contractual value date is today or has passed. Neither status confirms successful settlement.
 
Produced by: Produce the daily maturity population.
 
Used by: Trade Operations and Settlement Operations to review lifecycle eligibility and determine the required settlement preparation or follow-up.]]></documentation>
