      <dataStoreReference id="dataStoreReference_a8a366be-a19a-42f0-9f76-99f436539376"
                           name="SYS-FAP accounting/position state"
                           dataStoreRef="_a8a366be-a19a-42f0-9f76-99f436539376">
         <documentation id="documentation_a8a366be-a19a-42f0-9f76-99f436539376"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004; CSP-ST-001; CSP-ST-002.
Owner: SYS-FAP.
 
Consumers: Trade Operations and Settlement Operations.
 
Content: Accounting-position records, trade identifiers, accepted trade versions, contractual value dates, currencies, amounts and available lifecycle information relevant to maturity review.
 
Purpose: Provides the SYS-FAP position information used to identify the daily maturity population and review trade-version and lifecycle eligibility.
 
Usage: Read when producing and reviewing the maturity population. Compare the position information with the operational lifecycle tracker and available settlement instruction evidence before determining the required action.
 
A matured position or an accounting entry does not establish successful settlement. Instruction and leg-level settlement outcomes must be confirmed using SYS-SET and the relevant supporting evidence.]]></documentation>
