Owner: Relevant operational teams.
 
Consumers: Trade Operations and Settlement Operations; relevant exception owners and downstream control teams.
 
Content: Trade and accepted version references, currency-leg and instruction identifiers, observed operational statuses, outstanding exceptions, assigned owner, supporting evidence references, applicable cut-off impact, next action and follow-up time.
 
Purpose: Persistent operational record supporting maturity review, settlement preparation, submission reconciliation, settlement monitoring and exception resolution.
 
Usage: Read during population review and updated as preparation, submission, monitoring and recovery progress. Preserve confirmed settled-leg history and distinguish successful settlement from closure through cancellation, recall or recovery.
 
The tracker supports operational coordination. Authoritative instruction and settlement statuses remain in SYS-SET; cash recovery requires the corresponding cash movement evidence.]]></documentation>
