      <userTask name="Review submission results and confirm instruction references"
                 id="_1ff25c2a-172e-485b-a700-7f7a3d574066"
                 isForCompensation="false">
         <documentation id="documentation_1ff25c2a-172e-485b-a700-7f7a3d574066"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004;CSP-ST-004;CSP-ST-005;CSP-PR-008.
 
Input: Submitted settlement instruction details and the available SYS-SET instruction references and processing statuses.
 
Handling: Compare the intended instructions with the results available in SYS-SET. Confirm the correct trade, accepted version and currency-leg linkage, and record the separate identifier and current status for each expected leg.
 
Identify missing references, rejected instructions, duplicate or inconsistent records, and cases where only one leg has been successfully registered. Where a submission outcome is unclear, investigate the existing SYS-SET records before attempting resubmission.
 
Update the operational lifecycle tracker with the observed leg-level outcomes and any required follow-up.
 
Output: Reconciled submission outcomes for the expected currency legs, including confirmed instruction references and any unresolved submission exceptions. These results support subsequent settlement moinitoring and exception handling.
 ]]></documentation>
