      <userTask name="Determine the required settlement action"
                 id="_97e15635-bd6a-44e4-a343-7d3f1b25eb2e"
                 isForCompensation="false">
         <documentation id="documentation_97e15635-bd6a-44e4-a343-7d3f1b25eb2e"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004; CSP-PR-005; CSP-ST-002; CSP-ST-005.
 
Input: Maturity population reviewed by Trade Operations, operational lifecycle tracker, and existing SYS-SET settlement instructions and leg-level statuses.
 
Handling: Determine the required operational action for each trade using the lifecycle review outcome and the available instruction and settlement status for both currency legs.
 
Identify eligible trades requiring settlement preparation, trades with existing instructions requiring continued monitoring, and items requiring investigation because lifecycle or settlement information is inconsistent or incomplete.
 
Do not create duplicate instructions for trades already submitted for settlement. Preserve confirmed settled-leg outcomes and route outstanding or recovery-related items for the appropriate follow-up.
 
Output: Reviewed population classified by required settlement action, with the relevant trade, version, instruction references, and identified exceptions.]]></documentation>
