      <manualTask name="Investigate missing, rejected or inconsistent settlement instructions"
                   id="_a0168c29-71cf-404e-80b4-b99d3807fa32"
                   isForCompensation="false">
         <documentation id="documentation_a0168c29-71cf-404e-80b4-b99d3807fa32"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004; CSP-PR-005; CSP-ST-004; CSP-ST-007; CSP-PR-008.
 
Input: Missing, rejected, duplicated, incorrectly linked or unclear settlement instruction outcomes.
 
Handling: Compare the submitted details and submission evidence with existing SYS-SET records. Establish the actual state of both expected legs and determine the cause of the discrepancy. Coordinate clarification with the relevant operational or system-support owner and the counterparty where required.
 
Do not resubmit an instruction solely because an acknowledgement or reference is missing. Confirm whether the original instruction exists and whether correction or resubmission is required and safe. Preserve valid instructions and completed settlement history.
 
Continue checking the status of any existing valid instruction while investigating the affected leg.
 
Output: Documented investigation findings, current leg-level statuses, assigned owner and the required correction, resubmission, monitoring or escalation action.]]></documentation>
