      <inclusiveGateway name="Which settlement actions are required?"
                         id="_a30afb21-2c09-41fb-8021-61ab0b0820d4"
                         default="_c8576694-c16f-47ab-be67-dc9c32a5f86c">
         <documentation id="documentation_a30afb21-2c09-41fb-8021-61ab0b0820d4"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004; CSP-PR-005; CSP-ST-002; CSP-ST-005.
 
Decision basis: Settlement action classification produced by Determine the required settlement action.
 
Settlement preparation required: Route items requiring preparation or clarification of preparation-related data to settlement-detail validation. Unresolved lifecycle eligibility or incomplete settlement details must prevent progression to instruction preparation until resolved.
 
Existing instructions require monitoring: Route items with existing settlement instructions or unresolved questions about their existence or current status to settlement monitoring and the associated exception-handling path. Missing or uncertain evidence must not be interpreted as permission to create replacement instructions.
 
Different trades within the reviewed population may require different branches. Each branch handles only its assigned subset.
 
No action required: Use this default outcome only when the review confirms that no items require preparation, monitoring or exception follow-up. Uncertain or incomplete information does not qualify for this outcome.]]></documentation>
