      <exclusiveGateway name="What action is required to resolve the settlement exception?"
                         id="_af860abb-eae0-4e04-aa1d-aa3b3fd6318b"
                         gatewayDirection="Diverging">
         <documentation id="documentation_af860abb-eae0-4e04-aa1d-aa3b3fd6318b"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-005; CSP-ST-005; CSP-ST-007; CSP-PR-008.
 
Decision: Select the next action for the affected settlement case using the investigation findings and current leg-level statuses.
 
Monitoring can safely resume: The discrepancy has been explained and outstanding valid instructions can continue without an immediate correction or recovery action.
 
Safe instruction correction required: A specific instruction correction or submission action has been identified and can proceed to controlled preparation. This decision does not itself authorise resubmission.
 
Cancellation, recall or cash recovery required: The observed state requires cancellation, recall or recovery activity before the case can be resolved or normal monitoring can resume.
 
Resolution blocked - escalation required: The required action remains unclear, cannot safely proceed, or is prevented by the applicable cut-off or another unresolved dependency.
 
Preserve confirmed settled-leg history and valid instructions for unaffected legs throughout the selected action.]]></documentation>
