      <manualTask name="Prepare controlled correction or submission of affected instructions"
                   id="_e0fbcdf3-14ab-4b04-a521-0cd37c6f714c"
                   isForCompensation="false">
         <documentation id="documentation_e0fbcdf3-14ab-4b04-a521-0cd37c6f714c"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-004; CSP-ST-003; CSP-ST-004; CSP-ST-005; CSP-PR-008.
 
Input: Investigated submission or settlement exception, confirmed current instruction statuses and an identified correction or submission action.
 
Handling: Prepare and validate the required action for the affected instruction or instructions. Confirm the trade and accepted version, currency leg, amount, value date, settlement details and applicable cut-off. Establish whether the action concerns an amendment to an existing instruction or submission of a missing or replacement instruction. Before preparing a replacement, confirm that the original instruction cannot also settle. Preserve valid instructions for unaffected legs and all confirmed settlement history. Where those conditions cannot be established, route the case for escalation rather than resubmission.
 
Output: Validated correction or submission details identifying the affected legs, existing instruction references and the required action.]]></documentation>
         <extensionElements>
