      <manualTask name="Monitor settlement status of both currency legs"
                   id="_eacd7d9f-2870-4e49-93d5-9d338bf27b01"
                   isForCompensation="false">
         <documentation id="documentation_eacd7d9f-2870-4e49-93d5-9d338bf27b01"><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-005; CSP-ST-005; CSP-ST-006.
 
Input: Available instruction references and the latest available SYS-SET information for both expected currency legs, including any missing or uncertain instruction references or statuses requiring investigation.
 
Handling: Check the current status of each instruction independently in SYS-SET. Confirm trade, version and leg linkage, and review available settlement confirmations, rejection reasons and timing information against the applicable settlement window and cut-offs.
 
Preserve confirmed settlement history. Where one leg has settled and the other remains pending, determine whether the outstanding leg is progressing within the expected window or requires intervention.
 
Update the operational lifecycle tracker with the observed leg-level statuses and required follow-up.
 
Output: Current status evidence for both legs and an assessment of whether the trade is fully settled, remains pending without an exception, or requires exception handling.]]></documentation>
